             command line: build-windows.ps1 passes MTCapsApp, MTOutRoot,
               MTCapsLibsDir and MTBuildRoot with /p:, and a project reference
               inherits its parent's global properties;
             IDE: none of them is set, and the engine's Directory.Build.targets
               reads the app's name from $(SolutionDir)..\..\mtengine-app.conf.
           Both instances therefore carry the same globals, MSBuild builds the
           engine ONCE, and it lands where this project's link looks for it.

           Passing MTBuildRoot was doubly wrong after HANDOVER item 19 gave
           each app a static _ide\$(MSBuildProjectName)\ fallback: the app's
           own IDE build root travelled to the engine, whose output then moved
           under _ide\<App>\ where the solution never builds it. -->
